---
title: "issue_points_scoring (Sherlock Watsons)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_get_issue: for each valid issue in contest
    q_get_issue --> q_classify: determine severity
    q_classify --> q_high: severity = High
    q_classify --> q_medium: severity = Medium
    q_classify --> q_invalid: severity = Low or Informational
    q_invalid --> q_get_issue: skip, no points awarded
    q_high --> q_count_subs: count total submissions for this issue family
    q_medium --> q_count_subs: count total submissions for this issue family
    q_count_subs --> q_calc_weight: compute sybil-resistant weighting
    q_calc_weight --> q_high_formula: high_weight = 5 * (0.9 ^ (n - 1)) / n
    q_calc_weight --> q_med_formula: med_weight = 1 * (0.9 ^ (n - 1)) / n
    q_high_formula --> q_assign: assign weight to each submitter of this issue
    q_med_formula --> q_assign: assign weight to each submitter of this issue
    q_assign --> q_get_issue: next issue
    q_get_issue --> q_aggregate: all issues processed
    q_aggregate --> q_sum_watson: for each watson, sum all issue_points
    q_sum_watson --> q_calc_share: watson_share = watson_points / total_points
    q_calc_share --> q_calc_payout: watson_payout = watson_share * prize_pool
    q_calc_payout --> [*]: return payout per watson

    note right of q_calc_weight
        INV-001: High severity base weight = 5, Medium = 1
        INV-002: Formula = severity_factor * (0.9 ^ (submissions - 1)) / submissions
        INV-003: More unique findings yield higher per-person points (sybil resistance)
    end note

    note right of q_classify
        INV-004: Only Medium and High severity issues earn points
        INV-005: Low and Informational issues are excluded from scoring
    end note
